   "subject": "Posterior variance-covariance matrix of random effects in Besag spatial model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I was wondering if there was a way to obtain the posterior covariance or correlation between the spatially structured and unstructured random effects when fitting a Besag spatial model? For example, when fitting the model</div><div><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">form.mod<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\"> = </span>LBW<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\"> ~ Race</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">*Sex</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">+f(</span>County<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>model<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(176,22,0)\">&quot;iid&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>param<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=c(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(4,82,24)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(4,82,24)\">0.026</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">))+f(</span>County2<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">,</span>model<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(176,22,0)\">&quot;besag&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>graph<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span>Qmat.triangle<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>param<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=c(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(4,82,24)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(4,82,24)\">0.026</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">))</span></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">spat.mod<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">&lt;-inla(</span>form.mod<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>data<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span>births.data<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>family<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(176,22,0)\">&quot;binomial&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">,</span>Ntrials<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span><font color=\"#045218\">N</font><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">)</span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">I would like the posterior correlation between County and County2. </span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">Thanks,</span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">Michelle</span></font></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "RcaehbBmXM8J",
   "from": "Finn Lindgren",
   "author": "afb003e064114795",
   "date": "2013-11-13T16:57:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Posterior variance-covariance matrix of random effects in Besag spatial model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div>The full posterior correlation is a large dense matrix, so that can typically not be obtained in practice.</div><div><br></div><div>For a smaller number of count and and count2 combinations, you can use the &quot;lincomb&quot; features (see the FAQ), which allows computing the posterior correlation between linear combinations of latent variables.</div><div><br></div><div>Another option is to use sample from the posterior to calculate a Monte Carlo estimate of the correlations. (See recent discussion reads in the discussion groups for more information about using inla to sample from the posterior)</div><div><br></div><div>Finn<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div><br>On 13 Nov 2013, at 15:46, Michelle Ross &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mich...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I was wondering if there was a way to obtain the posterior covariance or correlation between the spatially structured and unstructured random effects when fitting a Besag spatial model? For example, when fitting the model</div><div><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">form.mod<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\"> = </span>LBW<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\"> ~ Race</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">*Sex</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">+f(</span>County<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>model<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(176,22,0)\">&quot;iid&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>param<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=c(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(4,82,24)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(4,82,24)\">0.026</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">))+f(</span>County2<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">,</span>model<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(176,22,0)\">&quot;besag&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>graph<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span>Qmat.triangle<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>param<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=c(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(4,82,24)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(4,82,24)\">0.026</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">))</span></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">spat.mod<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">&lt;-inla(</span>form.mod<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>data<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span>births.data<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">, </span>family<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(176,22,0)\">&quot;binomial&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">,</span>Ntrials<span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">=</span><font color=\"#045218\">N</font><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">)</span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">I would like the posterior correlation between County and County2. </span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">Thanks,</span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:4px;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(7,26,153)\">Michelle</span></font></p></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></blockquote></div>"
